# push_dashboard.py.patch — ONE cost basis for /positions P&L and Entry Price
#
# TARGET (the executing copy; AGENTS.md rule 4):
#     ~/.hermes/scripts/push_dashboard.py      repo: arshad1416/hermes-scripts
#   The pi-scripts/ copy in arshad1416/morning-briefing carries the same edit,
#   but editing it deploys nothing — this patch is what ships the fix.
#   Generated with `diff -u` against the live Pi copy, md5 88aa7889705b570d3ccf3c7e8c8310b3,
#   which was byte-identical to morning-briefing HEAD 74eb72e35 at the time.
#
# WHAT IT FIXES
#   The header tile and the per-row P&L used two different cost bases.
#   The header sums the ledger cost the engine actually debited from cash
#   (Sigma market_value - Sigma entry_value) and was always RIGHT. The rows
#   re-derived entry_price from a yfinance close on the entry date and computed
#   (current - that) x qty, so they never reconciled. The same wrong number was
#   published in the column labelled "Entry Price", which is an honest label over
#   a wrong value. The closed-trade loop had the identical defect, re-deriving
#   BOTH ends from yfinance instead of reading the booked fills and booked pnl.
#
# BEFORE / AFTER  (payload generated_at 2026-08-14 17:15:03)
#   header unrealized_pnl   425.07      425.07   (unchanged - it was correct)
#   Sigma of row pnl        361.67      425.07
#   GAP                     $63.40      $0.00
#     DIA  pnl  -35.04 -> -58.08   entry_price 538.99 -> 540.43
#     IWM  pnl  153.30 -> 267.00   entry_price 299.98 -> 296.19
#     XLK  pnl  173.43 -> 146.17   entry_price 186.32 -> 186.90
#     XLV  pnl  -56.71 (unchanged) KO pnl 126.69 (unchanged)  [same-day entries]
#   IWM pnl_pct 1.70 -> 3.00, moving its badge from "Up 0-2%" to "Up 2-5%".
#   Closed trades: closed_trades is EMPTY in the live ledger, so there is no
#   numeric before/after for that path today; it is fixed against the contract
#   paper_trading.py close_trade() writes.
#
# CURRENCY (verified read-only against ~/.hermes/skills/finance/scripts/paper_trading.py:794)
#   "entry_value": round(position_value * 100 * rate, 2) if trade_type == "option"
#                  else round(position_value, 2)          # position_value = qty * price
#   Stocks book entry_value = qty x NATIVE price, so entry_value/qty is exactly the
#   booked native fill (verified on all 5 live rows). OPTIONS book CAD with a 100x
#   multiplier, so entry_value/qty is NOT a price — but the open-positions options
#   branch is a separate code path that `continue`s before any line this patch
#   touches, so it is unaffected. The closed-trade loop is shared, so it reads the
#   ledger's per-unit entry_price/exit_price (native for both types) and uses
#   entry_value only as the pct denominator, where the 100x/rate cancels.
#   Nothing about how trades are BOOKED is changed — that is trading engine logic.
#
# ALSO REMOVED: get_entry_price() and to_native() lost their last callers with
#   this change (verified: nothing else on the Pi imports them; test_push_dashboard.py
#   imports only json_safe, update_prediction_accuracy.py only mentions the module in
#   a comment). They existed solely to compute the wrong basis, so they are deleted
#   rather than left for a third caller to find. `pandas as pd` goes with them.
#
